<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Katsina Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1348 CE – 1807 CE (approx.) · capital Katsina</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Hausa kingdom that became the leading commercial and scholarly city of Hausaland in the 17th and 18th centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Katsina was one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hausa-kingdoms">Hausa Bakwai</a>, the seven core <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa states</a>. Tradition says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammadu-korau">Korau</a>, a wrestler and newcomer, killed Sanau, the last ruler of the earlier Durbawa line, and founded a new dynasty in the 14th century. Muhammadu Korau, remembered as the first Muslim king and dated to the second half of the 15th century, is often identified with this founder, so the early chronology is uncertain.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Katsina stood at the southern end of a major trans-Saharan route through <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-agadez">Agadez</a> and became a centre of trade in cloth, leather, slaves and kola, and of Islamic learning, with scholars teaching at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobarau-minaret">Gobarau</a> mosque. It fought long wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> and acknowledged at times the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1807 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> jihadist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umaru-dallaji">Umaru Dallaji</a> captured the city, and Katsina became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/katsina-emirate">Katsina Emirate</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> royal family withdrew north and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-maradi">Sultanate of Maradi</a>, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/katsina-kingdom.jpg" alt="Katsina Kingdom" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Hosmich · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Hausa_people.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1348 CE – 1807 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Katsina</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammadu Korau</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hausa</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Katsina, Kingdom of Katsina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1578&amp;focus=katsina-kingdom" aria-label="Katsina Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4889 1694 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Katsina Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5209 1950L5144 1947M5209 1950L4999 1829M5209 1950L5399 1946M5209 1950L5209 1950M5209 1950L5195 1931"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5144 1947h0M4999 1829h0M5399 1946h0M5209 1950h0M5195 1931h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5209 1950h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5209 1950h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Katsina. <a href="/atlas?year=1578&amp;focus=katsina-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
